module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.DiagonalizableGroup
public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.AffineNormalQuotientGeometry
public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IsAlgClosed.Basic
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Finiteness
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheaf.Subscheme
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.RingHom.FaithfullyFlat

import Mathlib.RingTheory.Noetherian.Basic
import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Separated
import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.ClosedImmersion
import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Sites.Fpqc

/-! # Diagonalizable quotients and character kernels

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Theorem 12.9(b),(c), pp.233--234,
Definition 12.14, p.236, and Section 5(j), pp.116--118
(blueprint: lem-sfb-diagonalizable-quotient-character-kernel).

The coequalizer of the projection and the action is the pointwise coset presheaf.
The specified arrow from it to D(ker α) is its fppf sheafification universal arrow.
Equality of ideal sheaves identifies the scheme-theoretic image with the kernel;
it retains all nilpotents.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory Limits MonoidalCategory CartesianMonoidalCategory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The fppf cokernel of D(α) is D(ker α), via restriction of characters, and every
closed-subgroup quotient of D(M) is diagonalizable.

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Theorem 12.9(b),(c), pp.233--234,
Definition 12.14, p.236, and Section 5(j), pp.116--118
(blueprint: lem-sfb-diagonalizable-quotient-character-kernel).

Proof plan:
1. Put K = ker α and L = M/K. Subgroups of finitely generated abelian groups are
   finitely generated, by lem-weil-pbc-noetherian-submodule-finite over ℤ. The
   diagonalizable geometric criteria give affine finite-type group schemes;
   lem-weil-pbc-affine-source-morphism-separated gives separatedness.
2. The kernel of F[M] → F[L] is generated by e_k - 1 for k ∈ K: collect each finite
   sum by cosets of K and subtract one representative in each coset. The map
   F[L] → F[N] is injective on its basis. Thus D(L) is the scheme-theoretic image
   of D(α), using def-weil-closed-immersion.
3. On every F-algebra A, D(M)(A) = Hom(M,Aˣ), by def-weil-affine-spectrum.
   Restriction to K has kernel Hom(L,Aˣ), including nonreduced A. Hence its
   scheme-theoretic kernel is that same D(L).
4. Apply lem-sfb-algebraic-group-homomorphism-factorization to restriction and to
   D(N) → D(L). Their injective coordinate maps make the closed factors
   isomorphisms. Both maps are therefore faithfully flat and finitely presented.
5. The coset presheaves modulo D(N) and modulo D(L) have the same sheafification:
   the latter's representatives lift locally through the fppf map D(N) → D(L).
   Representable fpqc descent (lem-weil-pbc-fpqc-representable-descent) and the
   quotient map identify this sheafification with D(K), with the stated unit.
6. Embed D(M) in a split torus by choosing finite generators of M. Apply
   lem-sfb-split-torus-subgroups-diagonalizable to its arbitrary closed subgroup C,
   obtaining C ≅ D(P) for a finitely generated P, without reducedness assumptions.
7. By lem-sfb-multiplicative-character-antiduality the inclusion comes from a
   surjection β : M → P. Apply steps 1--5 to β. Commutativity makes C normal, so
   lem-sfb-affine-normal-quotient-geometry identifies this cokernel with D(M)/C.
   The zero group gives the group algebra F, so all these steps include it.
-/
theorem diagonalizable_quotient_character_kernel
    {F : Type u} [Field F] [IsAlgClosed F]
    (M N : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [AddCommGroup N]
    [AddGroup.FG M] [AddGroup.FG N] (α : M →+ N) :
    (diagonalizableGroupMap F α.ker.subtype).hom.hom.left.appTop.hom.FaithfullyFlat ∧
    (GrpObj.kerι (diagonalizableGroupMap F α.ker.subtype).hom.hom).left.ker =
      (diagonalizableGroupMap F α).hom.hom.left.ker ∧
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (Scheme.fppfTopology.over (Spec (.of F)))
      (yoneda.obj (diagonalizableGroup F α.ker).X) ∧
    (∃ ηq : coequalizer
        (yoneda.map (fst (diagonalizableGroup F M).X (diagonalizableGroup F N).X))
        (yoneda.map (diagonalizableGroupAction F α)) ⟶
          yoneda.obj (diagonalizableGroup F α.ker).X,
      coequalizer.π _ _ ≫ ηq =
        yoneda.map (diagonalizableGroupMap F α.ker.subtype).hom.hom ∧
      ∀ Z : Sheaf (Scheme.fppfTopology.over (Spec (.of F))) (Type u),
        Function.Bijective
          (fun f : yoneda.obj (diagonalizableGroup F α.ker).X ⟶ Z.obj ↦ ηq ≫ f)) ∧
    (∀ (C : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (i : C ⟶ diagonalizableGroup F M),
      IsClosedSubgroupScheme i.hom.hom →
      ∃ (P : Type u) (_ : AddCommGroup P) (_ : AddGroup.FG P)
        (q : diagonalizableGroup F M ⟶ diagonalizableGroup F P),
        IsFppfGroupQuotient i q) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
